{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfUSwGoAPLvVmJSgxTsXh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Add the second shift, don't buy the roaster yet. The month-to-month status of your two largest wholesale accounts is the swing factor: a $103K capex commitment (roaster + electrical) needs multiple years of sustained demand to pay back, but you don't yet know if the demand driving \"selling out\" is durable — if either account walks, you're stuck with expensive, underused equipment. The shift is reversible (a monthly cost you can turn off) and buys you a couple quarters to see if growth holds and to get those accounts onto longer-term contracts before locking in capital.\n\nMain tradeoff to watch: the shift accelerates wear on your only roaster and leaves you with no redundancy if it breaks down — so if demand keeps climbing and/or those accounts commit, revisit the second roaster then rather than defaulting to \"hold off\" indefinitely."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":40635,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c0760ef0-0b00-4626-9b35-74a6c2696bd2","uuid":"eb26d56a-2d36-4f21-b88a-8c378c74503d","timestamp":"2026-09-27T18:51:51.426Z","request_id":"req_011CfUSwGPbosjUS3KNS6vGs"}
